":"limited","t":"Key rotation (rotation period + manual Rotate key)","x":["The rotation period and next rotation time are stored and returned exactly as configured, but Vyomi has no background scheduler — it never rotates a key on its own; use \"Rotate key\" or wait for an external caller to do it."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.key.versions","l":"full","t":"Key versions (create, make primary, enable, disable, destroy, restore)","x":[]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.key.permissions","l":"limited","t":"Permissions (IAM policy on a key)","x":["setIamPolicy, :encrypt and :decrypt are enforced against the policy's bindings (an ungranted caller gets PERMISSION_DENIED; a caller with the matching predefined role — cryptoKeyEncrypterDecrypter/Encrypter/Decrypter/Viewer/admin — is let through). getIamPolicy and the key/version CRUD calls stay open to any caller, and conditions, custom roles, and org-policy constraints are not evaluated."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.crypto.symmetric","l":"full","t":"Encrypt / Decrypt","x":[]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.inventory","l":"full","t":"Key inventory (project-wide key search across all key rings and locations)","x":[]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.autokey","l":"limited","t":"Autokey (automatic per-resource key ring/key provisioning)","x":["AutokeyConfig (enable + key project) and CreateKeyHandle are real and enforced: a KeyHandle can only be created once Autokey is ACTIVE for the project, and creating one really provisions an \"autokey-{location}\" key ring and a brand-new CryptoKey (own key material) in the configured key project — not a stored reference."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.hsm-protection","l":"not_simulated","t":"HSM, External and External via VPC protection levels","x":["HSM keys are generated and held inside FIPS 140-2 Level 3 hardware modules and External keys live in a third-party key manager (EKM); Vyomi's key material always lives in its own software store, so offering these levels would misrepresent where the key is held."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.kms.import","l":"limited","t":"Key import (import jobs, wrapped key import)","x":["Symmetric 256-bit GOOGLE_SYMMETRIC_ENCRYPTION keys only, software protection only: import jobs mint a real RSA-3072/4096 wrapping key pair and cryptoKeyVersions:import really unwraps RSA-OAEP (SHA-1/SHA-256) + AES-KWP, but asymmetric/HMAC/RAW key import, HSM-backed jobs and attestation are not supported. Wrapping happens in pure Python on both substrates (no hardware key isolation)."]}],"id":"security/kms","ops":49,"registry_unreachable":[],"title":"Cloud KMS","total":83}
